data.content:
## What Changed

.NET 10's `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which targets **OpenAPI 3.1**. Key breaking changes affecting your code:

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. | Removed — use `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` |
| `schema.Example` is `IOpenApiAny` | `schema.Example` is `JsonNode` |
| `schema.Nullable = true/false` | Removed — use `schema.Type` flag: `JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` inherits `Dictionary<>` | Has a `Schemes` property instead |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;        // replaces Microsoft.OpenApi.Any
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // OpenApiString → JsonValue
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };
    // Dictionary initializer syntax no longer works; use Schemes property
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new()
        {
            Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
            {
                [oAuthScheme] = scopes
            }
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                // Nullable property removed; clear the Null flag from Type instead
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

### Summary of each fix

1. **`new OpenApiString("1.0")`** → `JsonValue.Create("1.0")` — all `OpenApiAny` types are replaced by `JsonNode`.
2. **`{ [scheme] = scopes }` initializer on `OpenApiSecurityRequirement`** → assign the `.Schemes` dictionary explicitly, since it no longer inherits from `Dictionary`.
3. **`property.Value.Nullable = false`** → `property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null` — OpenAPI 3.1 expresses nullability as a type union (`"type": ["string", "null"]`), so you toggle the `Null` flag on the `Type` enum.
